# CloudWatch Agent Setup for On-Prem Ubuntu

## Goal

Send system and custom metrics from an on-prem Ubuntu/WSL server to AWS CloudWatch.

Architecture:

Ubuntu / WSL
    ↓ HTTPS 443
AWS CloudWatch APIs
    ↓
CloudWatch Metrics

---

## 1. Configure AWS CLI

Verify:

```bash
aws --version
```

Configure credentials:

```bash
aws configure
```

Example:

AWS Access Key ID     = <access-key>
AWS Secret Access Key = <secret-key>
Region                = us-east-1
Output                = json
```

Verify authentication:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

---

## 2. IAM Permissions

The IAM user used by the on-prem server needs CloudWatch permissions.

For the CloudWatch Agent, AWS managed policy:

```text
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
```

was attached.

---

## 3. Test Custom Metric Manually

Publish a test metric:

```bash
aws cloudwatch put-metric-data \
  --namespace "OnPrem/Ubuntu" \
  --metric-name TestMetric \
  --value 1 \
  --dimensions Server=LAPTOP-HOO65F3F
```

Verify:

```bash
aws cloudwatch list-metrics \
  --namespace "OnPrem/Ubuntu"
```

Expected:

```text
Namespace  = OnPrem/Ubuntu
Metric     = TestMetric
Dimension  = Server=LAPTOP-HOO65F3F
```

---

## 4. Install CloudWatch Agent

```bash
cd /tmp

wget https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/ubuntu/amd64/latest/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb

sudo dpkg -i amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
```

Check:

```bash
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl -a status
```

Initially:

```text
status       = stopped
configstatus = not configured
```

---

## 5. Configure Credentials for On-Prem Agent

File:

```text
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/common-config.toml
```

Configuration:

```toml
[credentials]
shared_credential_profile = "default"
shared_credential_file = "/root/.aws/credentials"
```

Because this is not EC2, there is no EC2 IAM instance role.

The agent uses the AWS credentials file instead.

---

## 6. Configure Metrics

File:

```text
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/cloudwatch-agent.json
```

Example:

```json
{
  "agent": {
    "metrics_collection_interval": 60
  },

  "metrics": {
    "namespace": "OnPrem/Ubuntu",

    "metrics_collected": {
      "cpu": {
        "resources": ["*"],
        "measurement": [
          "usage_active",
          "usage_user",
          "usage_system",
          "usage_iowait"
        ],
        "totalcpu": true,
        "append_dimensions": {
          "Server": "LAPTOP-HOO65F3F"
        }
      },

      "mem": {
        "measurement": [
          "used_percent",
          "available_percent"
        ],
        "append_dimensions": {
          "Server": "LAPTOP-HOO65F3F"
        }
      },

      "disk": {
        "resources": ["/"],
        "measurement": [
          "used_percent",
          "free"
        ],
        "append_dimensions": {
          "Server": "LAPTOP-HOO65F3F"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Metrics collected:

```text
CPU
Memory
Filesystem/Disk
```

Collection interval:

```text
60 seconds
```

---

## 7. Start the Agent

```bash
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl \
  -a fetch-config \
  -m onPremise \
  -s \
  -c file:/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/cloudwatch-agent.json
```

Important:

```text
-m onPremise
```

tells the agent this is an on-premises machine.

---

## 8. Verify Agent

```bash
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl -a status
```

Expected:

```text
status       = running
configstatus = configured
```

Systemd:

```bash
systemctl status amazon-cloudwatch-agent
```

Logs:

```bash
tail -100 \
/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/logs/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.log
```

---

## 9. Verify Metrics

List metrics:

```bash
aws cloudwatch list-metrics \
  --namespace "OnPrem/Ubuntu"
```

Query memory directly:

```bash
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace "OnPrem/Ubuntu" \
  --metric-name mem_used_percent \
  --dimensions Name=Server,Value=LAPTOP-HOO65F3F \
  --statistics Average \
  --period 60 \
  --start-time "$(date -u -d '15 minutes ago' +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" \
  --end-time "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
```

